    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "Subset construction makes each DFA state a set of NFA states, using epsilon-closure and move.",
      "narration": "Subset construction removes nondeterminism. Each DFA state is a set of NFA states, found by following a character and taking the epsilon closure.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "h",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Subset construction",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "text": "S0 = eclosure({start})\nfor each DFA state S, char c:\n  T = eclosure(move(S, c))\n  if T is new: add it\n  delta[S][c] = T",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 18,
          "w": 84,
          "enter": "slide-up",
          "at": 1300
        },
        {
          "id": "n",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Worst case: 2^n DFA states.",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 46,
          "w": 84,
          "enter": "fade",
          "color": "orange",
          "at": 2100
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "Matching runs the DFA, remembering the last accepting position to get the longest match.",
      "narration": "Running the DFA costs one table lookup per character. Keep scanning until the dead state, remembering the last accepting position for the longest match.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "h",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Maximal munch",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "text": "state = 0; last = none\nfor each char c at pos:\n  state = delta[state][c]\n  if state == DEAD: break\n  if accepting[state]:\n    last = pos\nemit token up to last",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 18,
          "w": 84,
          "enter": "slide-up",
          "at": 1300
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "Tools like flex and re2c do this at build time and emit a ready-made scanner.",
      "narration": "Generators do this offline. Flex turns a rules file into lex.yy.c with compressed tables, and the DFA can be minimized to cut states.",
      "elements": [
